{
 "protocol": "Train the bundled success model on our own synthetic data and test it on an agent it never saw.\n\n    .venv/bin/python scripts/train_success_model.py            # train, evaluate, save\n    .venv/bin/python scripts/train_success_model.py --no-save  # only print the numbers\n\nProtocol (fixed before any SkyDesk number was looked at):\n  * TRAIN + SELECT : 600 synthetic ShopDesk runs (online-store support agent, two versions),\n                     build/samples/training/shopdesk_train_arl.jsonl, analysed with\n                     sample_logs/shopdesk_policy.yaml. Order-grouped 5-fold CV (every contact about\n                     one order stays in one fold). The feature set and L2 strength are chosen from the\n                     pre-listed candidates by ShopDesk CV AUC (ties -> lower Brier). SkyDesk plays no\n                     part in fitting or selection.\n  * TEST (once)    : 300 synthetic SkyDesk runs (airline agent: different domain, tools, policy, task\n                     mix and models), build/samples/skydesk_arl.jsonl with sample_logs/skydesk_policy.yaml.\n                     Reported for skydesk-v1, skydesk-v2 and all 300, for the chosen model only.\nThe fallback heuristic is scored on exactly the same runs.\nEvery fit uses sign constraints (model.EXPECTED_SIGNS: failure signals may only LOWER the chance of\nsuccess), so the per-run explanations never read backwards.\nBoth data sets are generated on the fly (deterministic, scripts/generate_sample_logs.py) into the\ngit-ignored build/samples/ when they are missing.",
